  "JUPITER_MOON_HINTS": {
    "Metis": "Orbits closer to Jupiter than any other known moon. Easy hint: five letters, starts with \"M\"",
    "Adrastea": "The smallest of Jupiter's four inner moons, and the first moon ever spotted in spacecraft images rather than through a telescope. Easy hint: eight letters, starts with \"Adr-\"",
    "Amalthea": "The largest of Jupiter's four inner moons, a reddish, potato-shaped body discovered in 1892. Easy hint: eight letters, starts with \"Ama-\"",
    "Thebe": "An inner moon marked by a giant crater named Zethus. Easy hint: five letters, one letter off from the ancient Greek city of Thebes",
    "Io": "The most volcanically active body in the solar system. Easy hint: just two letters, both vowels",
    "Europa": "An icy moon believed to hide a vast liquid ocean beneath its crust. Easy hint: one letter off from a continent",
    "Ganymede": "The largest moon in the solar system, bigger than the planet Mercury. Easy hint: eight letters, starts with \"Gany-\"",
    "Callisto": "The most heavily cratered object known in the solar system. Easy hint: eight letters, starts like \"call\"",
    "Themisto": "An irregular moon that orbits alone between the inner moons and the Himalia group. Easy hint: eight letters, starts with \"The-\"",
    "Leda": "The smallest member of the Himalia group, discovered in 1974. Easy hint: four letters, named for a queen in Greek myth visited by Zeus as a swan",
    "Himalia": "The largest of Jupiter's irregular moons. Easy hint: seven letters, sounds like the mountain range \"Himalayas\"",
    "Lysithea": "The second-smallest member of the Himalia group, discovered in 1938. Easy hint: eight letters, starts with \"Lys-\"",
    "Elara": "An irregular moon named for a mortal woman who bore Zeus's giant son, Tityus. Easy hint: five letters, starts and ends with the same letter",
    "Ananke": "Lends its name to a group of backward-orbiting moons; named for the Greek goddess of necessity. Easy hint: six letters, starts and ends with a vowel",
    "Carme": "The largest member of its backward-orbiting group, holding about 99 percent of that group's mass. Easy hint: five letters, one letter off from the name \"Carmen\"",
    "Pasiphae": "Lends its name to a group of irregular moons, and shares a name with the mythical mother of the Minotaur. Easy hint: eight letters, starts with \"Pas-\"",
    "Sinope": "Discovered in 1914, it was Jupiter's most distant known moon until 2000. Easy hint: six letters, starts with \"Sin-\"",
    "Callirrhoe": "One of the first irregular moons found by automated sky surveys, discovered in 1999. Easy hint: ten letters, the longest name in the quiz"
  },
